From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] P6 task 9: the workforce dashboard admin page

Adds the "Workforce" admin page (Sidebar entry + route + API call), gated
by the `workforce.view` permission exactly like 0039's Escalation Routing
page and 0041's Customer 360 page. Backs `GET /admin/workforce`
(`workforce_router.py`). The last table column is deliberately titled
"Availability history", never "Login/logout" -- it is derived from
PresenceEvent transitions to/from Chatwoot's native `offline` status only,
NOT a session record (see workforce_router.py's own module docstring and
ProtonWorkforceDashboardPage.vue's header comment for the full reasoning).

NOTE: this patch was hand-constructed against the last known state of these
three files (as left by 0045-dms-integration-card.patch, the most recent
patch to touch any of them -- 0046 through 0052 do not). This sandbox has
no network access to clone upstream/the fork, so this patch could NOT be
verified with `git apply --check` against a real checkout. The line numbers
in each hunk are inferred from 0045's own diff and may be off if some
later, unrelated patch touched these files in a way not visible from
grepping the patches directory; the context lines themselves are
transcribed verbatim from 0045's diff, which is what `git apply`'s own
offset-search primarily relies on to still apply cleanly. Flagging this
plainly per the task brief -- verify with a real `git apply --check` (or a
full `docker build` of the fork image) before relying on this in staging.
